- net
- pass
- desk

' A scope: a world that keeps places for other worlds and a catalog of the
' worlds that fill them. These are its rules, pure. Each reads the world as
' it stands and answers the writes that bring it one step on, and nothing
' when there is nothing to do, so a hand runs them whenever the world moves
' and they settle. Nothing here signs: an invitation is minted by the
' foot's desk when a place's record asks (desk.foil), and who a name is is
' read off the cards the foot keeps (pass.foil).
'
' A place is a record anywhere beneath a root, so a pack lays its places
' out as it likes: a seat in a list, a position in an office, a supplier
' of a project. What makes a record a place is that it holds an
' invitation's number in the slot invite. Without one it is only planned:
' whatever its maker wrote. It is open once the name minted for it is on
' it (name), and filled once a world stands in it (world). The catalog is
' <root>/catalog/<world>, one entry a world.
'
' A scope gives reach and nothing else. What it passes to a member about
' another is that world's founding, log and address; the member checks the
' first two against the name itself and takes only the address on the
' scope's word.
'
' A place is joined by a link. The scope that keeps the place says the
' link (linked): where the scope is reached, where the place's root sits
' there, and the minted name with its founding and first statement. With
' the invitation's secret after it, it is everything a world needs to take
' the place. A world handed a link asks its desk to claim the name (join)
' and, once that is done, meets the scope, takes its part and asks to be
' brought before it (joined). Nothing is taken on the link's word before
' the claim is made.
+ scope
  + link
    ' What a link to an invitation says, apart from its secret: the scope
    ' that keeps the place (to), its live key and where it is reached;
    ' where the place's root sits in that scope (rel); and the name minted
    ' for the place, with its founding and its first statement as it
    ' travels.
    : to=nat key=nat host=str port=nat rel=str name=nat made=pass/founding first=nat
  + show
    ' A link as one line of text: a number for the form, then each part,
    ' with commas between; the last four are the name's founding and
    ' first statement as a host starts a world with them (pass/birth).
    ' The invitation's secret, where it is given, follows as one part
    ' more.
    \ l=scope/link
    ^ str
    = parts=row[str] ["1" (nat/show l.to) (nat/show l.key) l.host (nat/show l.port) l.rel (nat/show l.name) (pass/birth l.made l.first)]
    | str/join "," parts
  + read
    ' A link from its text; none unless every part reads. A host or a
    ' root spelled with a comma is no link.
    \ text=str
    ^ maybe[scope/link]
    = none=maybe[scope/link] .none
      parts (str/split_byte 44 text)
    ? (and !(eq parts.len 11) !(eq parts.len 12)) none
    ? !(equal[str] parts.at(0) "1") none
    ?> (./some to) (nat/parse parts.at(1)) none
    ?> (./some key) (nat/parse parts.at(2)) none
    ?> (./some port) (nat/parse parts.at(4)) none
    ?> (./some name) (nat/parse parts.at(6)) none
    ?> (./some form) (nat/parse parts.at(7)) none
    ?> (./some custody) (nat/parse parts.at(8)) none
    ?> (./some dat) (nat/parse parts.at(9)) none
    ?> (./some first) (nat/parse parts.at(10)) none
    ?> (./some rel) (path_parse parts.at(5)) none
    | ./some (scope/link to key parts.at(3) port parts.at(5) name (pass/founding form custody dat) first)
  + secret
    ' The secret a link's text carries after its parts, or nothing.
    \ text=str
    ^ nat
    = parts (str/split_byte 44 text)
    ? !(eq parts.len 12) 0
    | (nat/parse parts.at(11)).fall(0)
  + beneath
    ' A path within a world: the same without the world it begins at.
    \ whole=path
    ^ path
    = none=path []
    % i=nat 1
      out=path none
    ^ path
    ? (ge i whole.len) out
    | _ i.inc out.snoc(whole.at(i))
  + placed
    ' The place beneath a root that holds an invitation's number; none
    ' when no record does.
    \ root=path id=nat state=namespace
    ^ maybe[path]
    = none=maybe[path] .none
    ? (eq 0 id) none
    | (sovereign_peek root state).tap.fold none
      \ acc [rel record]
      ? (maybe/is_some acc) acc
      ? (eq 0 rel.len) acc
      ? !(eq id record.nat_at(['invite] 0)) acc
      | ./some root.weld(rel)
  + linked
    ' The link to a place's invitation, as the scope that keeps the place
    ' says it. None until the place holds its name, and none while this
    ' world does not say where it is itself reached.
    \ root=path at=path state=namespace
    ^ maybe[scope/link]
    = none=maybe[scope/link] .none
      self state.self
      home=path [self 'io 'mesa]
    ?> (./some place) (sovereign_care .x at state).fil none
    ?> (./some mine) (sovereign_care .x home state).fil none
    = name place.nat_at(['name] 0)
      card=path [self 'io 'mesa ($x name)]
      host mine.txt_at(['host])
      port mine.nat_at(['port] 0)
      rel=path (scope/beneath root)
    ? (eq 0 name) none
    ? (eq 0 port) none
    ? (eq 0 host.len) none
    ?> (./some made) (pass/founded card state) none
    ?> (./some first) (pass/kept (pass/at card 1) state) none
    | ./some (scope/link (quip_val self) mine.nat_at(['key] 0) host port (path_show rel) name made (pass/sent (pass/of first)))
  + joining
    ' Where a world keeps the record of a joining, under the name the
    ' link gave it.
    \ self=iota name=nat
    ^ path
    [self 'io 'scope ($x name)]
  + claims
    ' Where the ask that claims a link's name is kept.
    \ self=iota name=nat
    ^ path
    = root (desk/root self)
    | root.weld(['join ($x name)])
  + brings
    ' Where the ask is kept that brings this world before a scope it
    ' joined under a name.
    \ self=iota name=nat
    ^ path
    = root (desk/root self)
    | root.weld(['bring ($x name)])
  + unlocked
    ' Whether a link may be handed to this world's door by nobody: only a
    ' link to this world's own name, and only while the world has let
    ' nobody in. Such a world was prepared for the link's place, and
    ' whoever holds the link's secret is whom it was prepared for. Any
    ' other link is handed over by someone the door let in.
    \ l=scope/link state=namespace
    ^ bool
    | and (eq l.name (quip_val state.self)) (desk/doorless state.self state)
  + join
    ' What a door writes when it is handed a link, having left the link's
    ' secret for the foot under a number (handed). The ask that claims
    ' the link's name is written, with the name's founding and first
    ' statement; and a record of the joining, which says what the link
    ' said of the scope and is acted on only once the claim is made
    ' (joined). A world claims its own name only when it was started
    ' under it, so that its card holds the name's log. session and until
    ' name the session the claim lets in, for a world that has let nobody
    ' in; 0 for none. Refused where this world has already joined under the
    ' name or holds the name's log past its first statement (the name is
    ' claimed), and while an earlier claim of the name is still waiting or
    ' the secret it was handed has not yet been cleared away, so two
    ' hand-overs never share the foot's one file.
    \ l=scope/link handed=nat session=nat until=nat state=namespace
    ^ either[iota row[[p=path q=writ]]]
    = self state.self
      me (quip_val self)
      home=path [self 'io 'mesa]
      at=path (scope/joining self l.name)
      ask=myth
        . (myth/sing ['want] (pails/t "claim"))
          put(['name] (pails/n l.name))
          put(['handed] (pails/n handed))
          put(['form] (pails/n l.made.form))
          put(['custody] (pails/n l.made.custody))
          put(['dat] (pails/n l.made.dat))
          put(['first] (pails/n l.first))
          put(['session] (pails/n session))
          put(['until] (pails/n until))
      record=myth
        . (myth/sing ['name] (pails/n l.name))
          put(['to] (pails/n l.to))
          put(['key] (pails/n l.key))
          put(['host] (pails/t l.host))
          put(['port] (pails/n l.port))
          put(['rel] (pails/t l.rel))
      asked=row[[p=path q=writ]] [[(scope/claims self l.name) (writ/make ask)] [at (writ/make record)]]
      named=path [self 'io 'mesa ($x l.name)]
      card=path (? (eq l.name me) home named)
      old (sovereign_care .x (scope/claims self l.name) state).fil.fall((myth/sing ['done] (pails/n 1)))
      waiting (eq 0 old.nat_at(['done] 0))
      unspent (and (gt old.nat_at(['handed] 0) 0) (eq 0 old.nat_at(['spent] 0)))
    ? (eq 0 l.name) (./err 'scope_link)
    ? (eq 0 l.to) (./err 'scope_link)
    ? (eq 0 handed) (./err 'scope_link)
    ? (gt (net/held ['maker] at state) 0) (./err 'scope_joined)
    ? (gt (net/held ['seq] card state) 1) (./err 'scope_joined)
    ? (waiting || unspent) (./err 'scope_busy)
    ? !(eq l.name me) (./ok asked)
    ? (maybe/is_some (pass/held home state)) (./ok asked)
    | ./err 'scope_unprepared
  + seated
    ' A joining whose claim is made takes its part. The scope the link
    ' named is met at the key and address the link gave, where this world
    ' keeps no card for it. The record takes what makes it a joining: the
    ' scope it is listed in, the composition it takes part in (maker,
    ' with rel), and where this world keeps what it writes of that
    ' (side): beneath mine, under the scope and where the root sits
    ' there, so two scopes' compositions never share a side.
    \ at=path record=myth state=namespace
    ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
    = self state.self
      to record.nat_at(['to] 0)
      peer=path [self 'io 'mesa ($x to)]
      nowhere=path []
      rel=path (path_parse record.txt_at(['rel])).fall(nowhere)
      base=path [self 'mine ($x to)]
      side=path base.weld(rel)
      card=myth
        . (myth/sing ['key] (pails/n record.nat_at(['key] 0)))
          put(['host] (pails/t record.txt_at(['host])))
          put(['port] (pails/n record.nat_at(['port] 0)))
      part=myth
        . (myth/sing ['maker] (pails/n to))
          put(['scope] (pails/n to))
          put(['side] (safe 0 .x side))
      only=row[[p=path q=writ]] [[at (writ/poke part)]]
      both=row[[p=path q=writ]] [[peer (writ/make card)] [at (writ/poke part)]]
    ? (net/live peer state) only
    both
  + joined
    ' One joining, one step. Nothing until the claim it asked for is
    ' made. Then it takes its part (seated). Then, once this world says
    ' where it is itself reached, it asks the desk to bring it before the
    ' scope: by the name it claimed, when that is not its own.
    \ at=path record=myth state=namespace
    ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
    = none=row[[p=path q=writ]] []
      self state.self
      me (quip_val self)
      name record.nat_at(['name] 0)
      to record.nat_at(['to] 0)
      home=path [self 'io 'mesa]
      ask=path (scope/brings self name)
      mine (sovereign_care .x home state).fil.fall(myth/new)
      port mine.nat_at(['port] 0)
      bring=myth
        . (myth/sing ['want] (pails/t "bring"))
          put(['to] (pails/n to))
          put(['by] (pails/n (? (eq name me) 0 name)))
          put(['host] (pails/t mine.txt_at(['host])))
          put(['port] (pails/n port))
      asked=row[[p=path q=writ]] [[ask (writ/make bring)]]
    ? (eq 0 name) none
    ? (eq 0 to) none
    ? !(eq 1 (net/held ['done] (scope/claims self name) state)) none
    ? (eq 0 record.nat_at(['maker] 0)) (scope/seated at record state)
    ? (net/live ask state) none
    ? (eq 0 port) none
    asked
  + asks
    ' Where the ask that mints a place's invitation is kept.
    \ self=iota id=nat
    ^ path
    = root (desk/root self)
    | root.weld(['invite ($u id)])
  + filler
    ' The world that fills a place whose invitation is the name n. It is n
    ' itself, once n has been claimed and has said where it runs. Or it is
    ' the world n's custody brought: one whose card holds an address and
    ' an introduction by n. None until one of them is heard.
    \ self=iota n=nat state=namespace
    ^ maybe[nat]
    = none=maybe[nat] .none
      card=path [self 'io 'mesa ($x n)]
      cards=path [self 'io 'mesa]
    ? (and (gt (net/held ['seq] card state) 1) (gt (net/held ['port] card state) 0)) (./some n)
    | (sovereign_peek cards state).tap.fold none
      \ acc [rel record]
      ? (maybe/is_some acc) acc
      ? !(eq rel.len 1) acc
      ? (eq 0 record.nat_at(['port] 0)) acc
      ?> (./some i) (pass/opened record.nat_at(['letter] 0)) acc
      ? !(eq i.by n) acc
      | ./some i.name
  + waits
    ' Whether a place admits only on approval.
    \ place=myth
    ^ bool
    | equal[str] place.txt_at(['terms]) "on approval"
  + tend
    ' One place, one step. A place with an invitation's number and no name asks the
    ' desk to mint its invitation, then takes the name the desk tells the
    ' ask. A place with a name and no world takes the world that fills it,
    ' when one is heard. A filled place is listed in the catalog: at once,
    ' or when its record says it is approved.
    \ root=path at=path state=namespace
    ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
    = none=row[[p=path q=writ]] []
      self state.self
    ?> (./some place) (sovereign_care .x at state).fil none
    = id place.nat_at(['invite] 0)
      name place.nat_at(['name] 0)
      world place.nat_at(['world] 0)
      ask (scope/asks self id)
      mint=row[[p=path q=writ]] [[ask (writ/make (myth/sing ['want] (pails/t "mint")).put(['id] (pails/n id)))]]
      entry=path root.weld(['catalog ($x world)])
      listing=row[[p=path q=writ]] [[entry (writ/make (myth/sing ['world] (pails/n world)).put(['place] (safe 0 .x at)))]]
    ? (eq 0 id) none
    ? (eq 0 name) (scope/named at ask mint state)
    ? (eq 0 world) (scope/taken at name state)
    ? (net/live entry state) none
    ? (and (scope/waits place) (eq 0 place.nat_at(['approved] 0))) none
    listing
  + named
    ' The ask that mints a place's invitation when there is none; the name
    ' onto the place once the desk has told the ask.
    \ at=path ask=path mint=row[[p=path q=writ]] state=namespace
    ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
    = none=row[[p=path q=writ]] []
    ?> (./some asked) (sovereign_care .x ask state).fil mint
    = told asked.nat_at(['name] 0)
      took=row[[p=path q=writ]] [[at (writ/poke (myth/sing ['name] (pails/n told)))]]
    ? (eq 0 told) none
    took
  + taken
    ' The world that fills a place, onto the place, when one is heard.
    \ at=path name=nat state=namespace
    ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
    = none=row[[p=path q=writ]] []
    ?> (./some found) (scope/filler state.self name state) none
    = took=row[[p=path q=writ]] [[at (writ/poke (myth/sing ['world] (pails/n found)))]]
    took
  + tended
    ' Every place beneath a root, one step each. A record with no
    ' invitation's number is not a place and is passed over.
    \ root=path state=namespace
    ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
    = none=row[[p=path q=writ]] []
    | (sovereign_peek root state).tap.fold none
      \ acc [rel record]
      ? (eq 0 rel.len) acc
      ? (eq 0 record.nat_at(['invite] 0)) acc
      | acc.weld((scope/tend root root.weld(rel) state))
  + listed
    ' The worlds a catalog lists.
    \ root=path state=namespace
    ^ row[nat]
    = none=row[nat] []
      catalog=path root.snoc('catalog)
    | (sovereign_peek catalog state).tap.fold none
      \ acc [rel record]
      ? !(eq rel.len 1) acc
      = w record.nat_at(['world] 0)
      ? (eq 0 w) acc
      | acc.snoc(w)
  + standing
    ' What of a card's own record a scope passes on: where the name
    ' stands and where it is reached.
    \ record=myth
    ^ myth
    . (myth/sing ['seq] (pails/n record.nat_at(['seq] 0)))
      put(['last] (pails/n record.nat_at(['last] 0)))
      put(['life] (pails/n record.nat_at(['life] 0)))
      put(['rift] (pails/n record.nat_at(['rift] 0)))
      put(['key] (pails/n record.nat_at(['key] 0)))
      put(['custody] (pails/n record.nat_at(['custody] 0)))
      put(['host] (pails/t record.txt_at(['host])))
      put(['port] (pails/n record.nat_at(['port] 0)))
  + public
    ' What of a card a scope passes on, as records beneath one name: the
    ' standing, the founding and the log. Not how a mount stands, not an
    ' introduction, and nothing else the card keeps.
    \ card=path state=namespace
    ^ row[[rel=path record=myth]]
    = none=row[[rel=path record=myth]] []
    | (sovereign_peek card state).tap.fold none
      \ acc [rel record]
      ? (eq rel.len 0) acc.snoc([rel (scope/standing record)])
      ? !(eq_iota rel.at(0) 'pass) acc
      | acc.snoc([rel record])
  + tell
    ' What a scope writes into one member's root: every other listed
    ' world, as far as it may be passed on, beneath catalog/<world>. Only
    ' what differs from what is there is written, so telling again when
    ' nothing moved writes nothing.
    \ root=path member=nat state=namespace
    ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
    = self state.self
      none=row[[p=path q=writ]] []
      base=path [self 'our ($x member)]
      fresh=row[[p=path q=writ]] [[base (writ/make myth/new)]]
      head (? (net/live base state) none fresh)
    | (scope/listed root state).fold head
      \ out=row[[p=path q=writ]] w=nat
      ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
      ? (eq w member) out
      = card=path [self 'io 'mesa ($x w)]
        at=path base.weld(['catalog ($x w)])
      | (scope/public card state).fold out
        \ acc=row[[p=path q=writ]] item=[rel=path record=myth]
        ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
        = [rel record] item
          target=path at.weld(rel)
        ? (equal[myth] record (sovereign_care .x target state).fil.fall(myth/new)) acc
        | acc.snoc([target (writ/make record)])
  + told
    ' The catalog as every listed member is told it.
    \ root=path state=namespace
    ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
    = none=row[[p=path q=writ]] []
    | (scope/listed root state).fold none
      \ out=row[[p=path q=writ]] member=nat
      ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
      | out.weld((scope/tell root member state))
  + take
    ' At a member: the worlds a scope lists become cards of this world's
    ' own, one step each. A name not yet met is met: the founding and log
    ' the scope passed on are checked against the name, as at any first
    ' contact, and the address is kept on the scope's word. A name already
    ' met takes the next statement the scope shows, by the log's own rule.
    \ scope=nat state=namespace
    ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
    = self state.self
      none=row[[p=path q=writ]] []
      from=path [self 'her ($x scope) 'catalog]
    | (sovereign_peek from state).tap.fold none
      \ acc [rel record]
      ? !(eq rel.len 1) acc
      ? (eq_iota rel.at(0) self) acc
      = card=path [self 'io 'mesa rel.at(0)]
      | acc.weld((scope/met card from.weld(rel) record state))
  + met
    ' One listed world, one step.
    \ card=path entry=path shown=myth state=namespace
    ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
    = none=row[[p=path q=writ]] []
    ?> (./some made) (pass/founded entry state) none
    ?> (./some stands) (pass/held card state) (scope/first card entry made shown state)
    ? (ge stands.seq shown.nat_at(['seq] 0)) none
    ?> (./some next) (pass/kept (pass/at entry stands.seq.inc) state) none
    ?> (./ok writes) (pass/turn card (pass/of next) state) none
    writes
  + first
    \ card=path entry=path made=pass/founding shown=myth state=namespace
    ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
    = none=row[[p=path q=writ]] []
    ?> (./ok writes) (pass/meet_at card made (pass/log entry state) shown.txt_at(['host]) shown.nat_at(['port] 0) state) none
    writes
